{% comment %}
  One row of the event list.

  Extracted so the two sources -- a Seminars collection and hand-authored
  blocks -- render identically. Duplicating the markup in both branches is how
  the fallback quietly stops matching the real thing.

  Every value arrives already resolved. The snippet makes no decisions about
  where a row points or what it costs; it only draws.

    city        string, required
    date        string, already formatted for display
    focus       string, blank renders the TBA state
    price       string, already money-formatted
    target      href. Ignored when sold_out
    sold_out    boolean. Renders a <div>, not a link
    cue         link text, defaults to "Reserve"
    attrs       block.shopify_attributes, or blank in collection mode
{% endcomment %}

{%- if sold_out -%}
  <div class="suf-semrow" {{ attrs }}>
{%- else -%}
  <a class="suf-semrow" href="{{ target | default: '#' }}" {{ attrs }}>
{%- endif -%}

<span class="suf-semrow__city">{{ city | escape }}</span>
<span class="suf-semrow__date">{{ date | escape }}</span>

{%- comment -%}
  Cities are announced before their focus is decided, so an empty value is a
  normal state rather than a missing one. Left bare it rendered as a blank cell
  in the middle of the row, which reads as broken rather than as pending.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if focus != blank -%}
  <span class="suf-semrow__focus">{{ focus | escape }}</span>
{%- else -%}
  <span class="suf-semrow__focus suf-semrow__focus--tba">Focus TBA</span>
{%- endif -%}

<span class="suf-semrow__price">{{ price }}</span>

{%- if sold_out -%}
  <span class="suf-semrow__focus">Sold out</span>
{%- else -%}
  <span class="suf-semrow__cue">
    {{- cue | default: 'Reserve' | escape }}
    <span class="suf-semrow__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
  </span>
{%- endif -%}

{%- if sold_out -%}</div>{%- else -%}</a>{%- endif -%}
